      "content": "i hear you. but some of our developers are worried that if we optimize purely for outcome, it might actually end up being unfair to individuals who have a high creditworthiness based on their actual financial history. they're arguing that 'equality of opportunity' is a better metric. wouldn't optimizing for outcome basically be ignoring real risk and making the system less accurate?",
